<spell-notebook "rail theming">
	<header level="1">
		Rail
		<header>A rail is used to show accompanying content outside the boundaries of the main view of a
              site.</>
	</>
	<rail-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-rail-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or on the
			rail's box through `::part(rail)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a private
			alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- `--ui-rail-width` is Fomantic's 300px; `close` and `dividing` rails add their own distance to it.
			- `--ui-rail-distance` is the gap to the container, split between the rail's margin and padding.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every rail on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-rail-width: 240px;
			}
			/* one layout */
			.docs-page {
			  --ui-rail-distance: 2em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`close` and `dividing` replace the distance with their own tokens (`--ui-rail-close-distance`,
				`--ui-rail-dividing-distance` ...). Never set the `--_ui-rail-*` / `--_rail-*` names: they're the sheet's private
				plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-rail" playground>
				<div style="margin-inline: 20em">
					<ui-segment>
						<ui-rail position="left">
							<ui-segment>Left rail content</>
						</>
						<ui-rail position="right">
							<ui-segment>Right rail content</>
						</>
						<p>Main content. Te eum doming eirmod, nominati pertinacia argumentum ad his.</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>A rail has no look of its own:  a theme changes what it holds.</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
